    },

    "NitiaDock just lost its Accessibility permission, so the taskbar has been put away. Turn NitiaDock back on in %@.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "NitiaDock just lost its Accessibility permission, so the taskbar has been put away. Turn NitiaDock back on in %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Couldn’t start a new instance of NitiaDock: %@\n\nYou can click Retry, or quit and open it manually from your Applications folder.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Couldn’t start a new instance of NitiaDock: %@\n\nYou can click Retry, or quit and open it manually from your Applications folder."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Some items can’t be accessed. Allow NitiaDock to access their folder in your Mac’s privacy settings.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Some items can’t be accessed. Allow NitiaDock to access their folder in your Mac’s privacy settings."
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "macOS Dock (⌥⌘D to show/hide)": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS Dock (⌥⌘D to show/hide)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Moves or shrinks the front window when it would end up under the taskbar. Only while the taskbar is always visible. Windows are not moved back when you turn this off.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Moves or shrinks the front window when it would end up under the taskbar. Only while the taskbar is always visible. Windows are not moved back when you turn this off."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "NitiaDock needs it to show your windows and switch between them.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "NitiaDock needs it to show your windows and switch between them."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Turn on NitiaDock in %@. This window closes by itself once you do, and the taskbar appears.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Turn on NitiaDock in %@. This window closes by itself once you do, and the taskbar appears."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "macOS ties Accessibility permission to one specific copy of an app. This copy is running from a temporary or read-only location, so turning the switch on will not take effect — and the permission record stays behind in System Settings after the disk image is ejected. Drag NitiaDock to your Applications folder and open it from there.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS ties Accessibility permission to one specific copy of an app. This copy is running from a temporary or read-only location, so turning the switch on will not take effect — and the permission record stays behind in System Settings after the disk image is ejected. Drag NitiaDock to your Applications folder and open it from there."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If the switch is already on and nothing happens, a permission record left by an older version may no longer match this copy of NitiaDock. You can reset it:\n\n1. Quit NitiaDock first — while it is running, the minus button in the list is greyed out and the entry cannot be removed.\n2. In Privacy & Security > Accessibility, select NitiaDock in the list and remove it with the minus button. There may be more than one entry; remove them all.\n3. Open NitiaDock again from your Applications folder, then add it and turn the switch on when prompted.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "If the switch is already on and nothing happens, a permission record left by an older version may no longer match this copy of NitiaDock. You can reset it:\n\n1. Quit NitiaDock first — while it is running, the minus button in the list is greyed out and the entry cannot be removed.\n2. In Privacy & Security > Accessibility, select NitiaDock in the list and remove it with the minus button. There may be more than one entry; remove them all.\n3. Open NitiaDock again from your Applications folder, then add it and turn the switch on when prompted."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "\n\nIf simply turning the switch back on works, NitiaDock restarts itself and there is nothing else to do; going through the cleanup above means reopening it manually afterwards.\nAlso, windows the taskbar had moved out of its way may sit one taskbar height short — maximizing them once puts them back.": {
      "comment": "fork: NitiaDock",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "\n\nIf simply turning the switch back on works, NitiaDock restarts itself and there is nothing else to do; going through the cleanup above means reopening it manually afterwards.\nAlso, windows the taskbar had moved out of its way may sit one taskbar height short — maximizing them once puts them back."
          }
        }
      }
    },

